U('installation-guide',1,'安装文档里的前提与步骤','安装指南',[
 ['Before installing the command-line client, check that your operating system is listed under Supported platforms. The installer does not include the runtime required by the client. If the runtime is missing, install a supported version first, then close and reopen your terminal. An already open terminal may continue to use its previous environment, so a successful installation does not necessarily make the new command available there immediately.','安装命令行客户端前，请确认你的操作系统列在“支持的平台”中。安装程序不包含客户端需要的运行环境。如果缺少它，请先安装受支持的版本，再关闭并重新打开终端。已经打开的终端可能继续使用原先的环境，因此安装成功不一定会让新命令立即在那个终端中可用。'],
 ['Download the package for your system and follow the installation instructions. Do not choose a package solely because its file name contains the newest version number; its architecture must also match your device. After installation, run the version command shown below the download link. The output should contain the client name and the version you intended to install. This check confirms that the terminal can find the client, but it does not test whether a remote server is reachable.','下载适合系统的软件包并按说明安装。不要仅因为文件名含最新版本号就选择它，架构也必须与设备匹配。安装后，运行下载链接下显示的版本命令，输出应包含客户端名称和你想安装的版本。这个检查能确认终端找得到客户端，但不会测试远程服务器能否连接。'],
 ['If the command is not found, open a fresh terminal before changing other settings. If the problem remains, include your system, architecture and installation method when asking for help. Copy the exact error text rather than describing every failure as “it does not work”.','如果提示找不到命令，在调整其他设置之前先开一个新终端。如果问题仍在，求助时请提供系统、架构和安装方式。复制准确错误文本，不要把所有故障都描述为“用不了”。']
],[['supported platform','受支持的平台','Check the list of supported platforms.'],['runtime','运行环境','Install the required runtime first.'],['not necessarily','不一定','A successful install does not necessarily update an open terminal.'],['architecture','架构','Choose the package for your device architecture.'],['reachable','可以连接到的','The server is not reachable from this network.']],[[
 '为什么安装后可能需要重新打开终端？',['旧终端可能保留原有环境','终端必须每天重装','版本检查会删除配置'],0,'第一段解释 already open terminal 可能继续使用 previous environment。'],['版本命令成功是否证明服务器能连接？',['证明','不证明，只检查客户端能否找到','证明所有配置都正确'],1,'第二段区分本地命令可用与远端可达。'],['安装包只看版本号就够了吗？',['够','不够，还要核对架构等支持条件','只要文件最大就行'],1,'文中用 solely 排除只看版本号的做法。']
],{task:'写一段安装后的故障求助：安装显示成功，但终端找不到命令。',audience:'项目支持社区',length:'100～150 词',requirements:['交代系统、架构和安装方式，可使用虚构信息','说明是否重新打开过终端以及结果','提供准确错误，并区分本地问题与服务器问题'],starter:'Environment:\nWhat I did:\nWhat I observed:',model:'I installed the command-line client on a 64-bit training system using the package linked in the installation guide. The installer reported success, but entering the version command produced “command not found”. I closed the terminal and opened a fresh one, then tried the same command again. The result was unchanged. I also checked that I had downloaded the package for the correct system and architecture. I have not tested a server connection because I cannot run the client yet. Could you suggest how to check whether the installation directory is available to the terminal? I can provide the installer log if needed.'});
U('command-output',1,'命令执行成功，任务也成功了吗','命令行文档',[
 ['The check command examines configuration files without changing them. By default, it prints a short summary to standard output and sends diagnostic details to standard error. Both streams may appear in the same terminal window, so the presence of text on the screen does not tell you which stream it came from. When saving output for a report, check whether your method captures both streams or only one.','check 命令检查配置文件，但不修改它们。默认情况下，它向标准输出打印简短摘要，向标准错误发送诊断详情。两种输出流可能显示在同一个终端窗口中，因此仅凭屏幕上有文字，无法判断来自哪一条流。为报告保存输出时，请确认方法捕获两条流还是仅一条。'],
 ['In this tool, an exit code of zero means that the check completed and no invalid configuration was found. A code of one means that the check completed but found at least one problem. A code of two means that the command could not finish the check, for example because it could not read a file. These meanings belong to this tool; another program may use different codes. Do not assume that a readable summary means every file passed.','在这个工具中，退出码零表示检查完成且没有发现无效配置；一表示检查完成但发现至少一个问题；二表示命令未能完成检查，例如无法读取文件。这些含义只属于此工具，其他程序可能使用不同代码。不要以为看到了可读摘要就表示每个文件都通过。'],
 ['For an automated workflow, inspect the exit code as well as the saved output. If the check could not finish, report that limitation separately from any configuration problems already detected. “No additional errors were reported” is not the same as “all files were checked successfully”.','在自动化流程中，除了保存输出，还要检查退出码。如果检查未完成，请将这个限制与已经发现的配置问题分开报告。“没有报告更多错误”不同于“所有文件均已成功检查”。']
],[['standard output','标准输出','The summary is written to standard output.'],['standard error','标准错误','Diagnostics are sent to standard error.'],['exit code','退出码','Inspect the exit code after the command finishes.'],['at least one','至少一个','The check found at least one problem.'],['could not finish','未能完成','The command could not finish the check.']],[[
 '此工具的退出码一表示什么？',['程序完全无法启动','检查完成并发现问题','所有文件无问题'],1,'第二段分别定义了零、一、二。'],['这些退出码的含义能直接套用到所有程序吗？',['能','不能，要查具体工具文档','只能套用到所有图形应用'],1,'These meanings belong to this tool 是范围限制。'],['为何不能把“没报告更多错误”当成“全部通过”？',['可能有文件根本没检查完','因为文本没有颜色','因为标准输出不允许有摘要'],0,'最后一段提醒检查不完整的情况。']
],{task:'向同事报告一次配置检查：发现一个问题，同时有一个文件无法读取。',audience:'维护自动化流程的同事',length:'100～150 词',requirements:['区分检查发现的问题与未完成的检查','说明要保留输出和退出码','避免把没有其他报错写成全部通过'],starter:'The configuration check…\nHowever, it could not…',model:'The configuration check reported one invalid setting in the sample project. However, it could not read a second file, so the overall check is incomplete. I have saved the diagnostic output and recorded the exit code. In this tool, code two indicates that the check could not finish; it should not be treated as a successful result. We need to investigate the unreadable file and run the check again after resolving the access problem. At present, I can confirm the reported setting error, but I cannot confirm that every other file is valid. I will attach both the summary and the diagnostic details to the report.'});
U('release-notes',1,'更新说明：新增、修复与已知问题','版本说明',[
 ['Version 3.2 adds a search box to the project list and fixes a problem that caused the selected sort order to be lost after a restart. Existing projects do not need to be converted. The search box filters project names only; it does not search the contents of project files. If you cannot find a project by typing a word from one of its documents, that does not necessarily indicate a search failure.','3.2 版在项目列表中增加搜索框，并修复重启后所选排序方式丢失的问题。现有项目不需要转换。搜索框只筛选项目名，不搜索项目文件内容。如果输入文档里的某个词却找不到项目，不一定意味着搜索功能故障。'],
 ['There is one known issue in this release. When a project is stored on a disconnected external drive, its last opened date may appear blank. The project itself is not removed. Reconnect the drive and reopen the project to refresh the date. We plan to improve this behaviour, but no delivery date has been confirmed. Please do not rely on an estimated date mentioned in an earlier discussion as a release commitment.','此版本有一个已知问题：项目存放在已断开连接的外置盘上时，最近打开日期可能为空。项目本身并未被移除。重新连接硬盘并打开项目可以刷新日期。我们计划改善这个行为，但尚未确认交付日期。请不要将早先讨论里提到的预估日期视为发布承诺。'],
 ['Before reporting a problem, include the exact version number and check whether it matches the known issue above. Similar symptoms may have different causes, so include the steps you followed even if another report looks familiar.','报告问题前，请提供准确版本号，并检查是否符合上述已知问题。相似症状可能有不同原因，因此即使另一份报告看起来很熟悉，也请提供你实际执行的步骤。']
],[['sort order','排序方式','The app now remembers the sort order.'],['known issue','已知问题','Check the known issues before reporting a bug.'],['disconnected','已断开连接的','The project is on a disconnected drive.'],['delivery date','交付日期','No delivery date has been confirmed.'],['release commitment','发布承诺','An estimate is not a release commitment.']],[[
 '搜索框搜索什么？',['所有文件内容','仅项目名','整个系统设置'],1,'第一段用 only 限定范围。'],['外置盘断开时日期空白，是否证明项目被删除？',['证明','不证明','证明所有文件损坏'],1,'第二段明确说项目本身未移除。'],['计划改善是否等于确认了发布日期？',['是','不是','只要讨论过日期就是承诺'],1,'文中区分 plan、estimate 和 commitment。']
],{task:'给团队写简短更新摘要，区分已发布功能与尚未确定的修复计划。',audience:'即将升级的团队成员',length:'100～150 词',requirements:['概括新增搜索与排序修复','说明搜索范围和已知问题','避免承诺未确认的交付日期'],starter:'Version 3.2 is available…\nPlease note that…',model:'Version 3.2 is available and adds a search box to the project list. It also fixes the problem where the selected sort order was lost after restarting. Existing projects do not need conversion. Please note that the new search filters project names, not document contents. One known issue remains: projects on disconnected external drives may show a blank last opened date. This does not mean that the project was deleted. Reconnecting the drive and reopening the project should refresh the date. An improvement is planned, but its release date has not been confirmed. Please include your exact version and reproduction steps if you report a similar problem.'});
U('deprecated-option',1,'Deprecated 并不是立刻不能用','迁移说明',[
 ['The legacy-format option is deprecated in the current release. It still works, but new integrations should use output-format instead. Deprecation is advance notice that an interface is being replaced; it does not necessarily mean the old interface has already been removed. In this project, legacy-format is scheduled for removal in the next major release. Minor updates to the current major version will continue to accept it.','legacy-format 选项已在当前版本中弃用。它仍可工作，但新集成应使用 output-format。弃用是接口将被替代的提前通知，不一定意味着旧接口已经移除。在这个项目中，legacy-format 计划在下一个主版本移除，当前主版本的小版本更新仍接受它。'],
 ['The replacement is not a simple change of name. The old option accepts true or false, while the new option accepts one of three named formats. Read the migration table and choose the format that preserves the behaviour your users expect. If both options are provided, this version reports an error rather than silently choosing one. Update any examples and configuration templates as well as the code that reads them.','替代方案不只是改名。旧选项接受 true 或 false，新选项接受三种格式名称之一。请阅读迁移对照表，并选择能保留用户预期行为的格式。如果两个选项同时提供，此版本会报错，而不是默默选择其中一个。除了读取配置的代码，也要更新示例和配置模板。'],
 ['Before upgrading to the next major version, test a representative set of existing configurations. A passing test for the new default does not show that every old configuration has been migrated. Keep a record of which cases you checked and which still need attention.','升级下一个主版本前，请测试一组有代表性的现有配置。新默认值的测试通过，并不能证明每个旧配置都已完成迁移。记录检查过哪些情况，以及哪些仍需处理。']
],[['deprecated','已弃用的','The old option is deprecated but still accepted.'],['major release','主版本发布','The option will be removed in the next major release.'],['preserve the behaviour','保留原有行为','Choose a format that preserves the behaviour.'],['rather than silently','而不是默默地','The tool reports an error rather than silently choosing.'],['representative','有代表性的','Test representative configurations.']],[[
 '此处 deprecated 意味着什么？',['已替代但当前仍可用','所有版本已彻底删除','永远不会删除'],0,'第一段明确说明 still works，并给出未来移除计划。'],['能只把旧选项名称改掉吗？',['可以，新旧值完全相同','不能，还要映射不同的取值','只需同时保留两个选项'],1,'第二段对比布尔值和格式名称。'],['新默认配置通过测试说明了什么？',['所有旧配置都已迁移','只说明测试覆盖的那个情况通过','说明无需更新模板'],1,'末段限制了从单次通过推断整体完成的范围。']
],{task:'写一份升级前的迁移提醒。',audience:'维护已有集成的开发者',length:'110～160 词',requirements:['解释弃用与移除的区别','指出取值变化和双选项冲突','安排旧配置及模板的检查'],starter:'The current release still accepts…\nBefore the next major upgrade,…',model:'The current release still accepts legacy-format, but the option is deprecated and scheduled for removal in the next major version. New integrations should use output-format. This is more than a rename: the old option uses a Boolean value, while the new one requires a named format. Please use the migration table to preserve the expected behaviour. Do not leave both options in a configuration, because the tool will report an error. Before the next major upgrade, check existing configurations, examples and templates. We should test representative cases rather than relying only on the new default. Please record any cases that have not yet been migrated so we can resolve them before upgrading.'});
U('pagination-guide',1,'为什么第一页不是全部结果','API 文档',[
 ['The list endpoint returns results in pages. A response contains up to fifty records and may include a next_cursor value. If that value is present, send it with your next request to continue from the same position. If it is absent, there are no further pages in that result sequence. A response containing fewer than fifty records may still include a cursor, so the number of records alone is not a reliable stopping rule.','列表接口分页返回结果。一个响应包含最多五十条记录，并且可能带有 next_cursor 值。存在该值时，请将它附在下次请求中，从相同位置继续。如果没有这个值，表示这次结果序列没有后续页面。少于五十条记录的响应仍可能带游标，因此仅凭记录数量不能可靠地决定是否停止。'],
 ['Treat the cursor as an opaque value. Do not extract a record number from it or construct a new cursor yourself. Use the same filters throughout a sequence of requests; changing filters while reusing a cursor can produce an invalid request. If you need a different filter, begin a new sequence without a cursor.','请将游标视为不应自行解释的值。不要从中提取记录编号，也不要自行构造新游标。在同一请求序列中使用相同过滤条件；更改过滤条件却复用游标可能产生无效请求。如果需要不同过滤条件，请从不带游标的新序列开始。'],
 ['This endpoint does not promise a fixed snapshot across pages. Records may change while you are fetching them. For a report that requires a stable point-in-time view, use the export feature described separately. Pagination tells you how to continue reading results; it does not, by itself, guarantee that the underlying data stayed unchanged.','此接口不保证各页对应同一个固定快照。获取过程中记录可能变化。如果报告需要稳定的某一时刻视图，请使用另行说明的导出功能。分页说明了如何继续读取结果，本身并不保证底层数据保持不变。']
],[['up to','最多','A response contains up to fifty records.'],['further pages','后续页面','There are no further pages.'],['opaque value','不应自行解释的值','Treat the cursor as an opaque value.'],['throughout','自始至终；贯穿','Use the same filters throughout the sequence.'],['point-in-time view','某一时刻的视图','The report requires a stable point-in-time view.']],[[
 '少于五十条记录就能停止了吗？',['能','不能，应检查 next_cursor','必须永远继续'],1,'第一段明确指出记录数量不是可靠停止条件。'],['更改过滤条件后应该怎样？',['继续复用原游标','自行把游标加一','不带游标开始新序列'],2,'第二段给出新序列的起始方式。'],['分页是否保证数据是固定快照？',['保证','不保证，稳定报告需另查导出功能','只要每页五十条就保证'],1,'第三段区分页读取机制与快照一致性。']
],{task:'向同事说明如何完整获取列表，以及为什么不能将它当作固定快照。',audience:'调用此模拟 API 的同事',length:'110～160 词',requirements:['说明游标继续与停止规则','说明过滤条件不能中途随意更换','指出快照限制和可查的替代功能'],starter:'To retrieve the complete sequence,…\nHowever, pagination does not…',model:'To retrieve the complete sequence, keep requesting pages while the response includes next_cursor. Send the returned value unchanged with the next request. Do not stop merely because a page contains fewer than fifty records. The cursor should not be interpreted or constructed manually. Keep the same filters for the entire sequence; if we need different filters, we should start again without a cursor. However, pagination does not provide a fixed snapshot in this API. Records may change while we are fetching them. If the report requires a stable view of a particular moment, we need to investigate the separate export feature rather than assuming that a completed page sequence meets that requirement.'});
U('retry-request',1,'遇到请求限制，先等还是重试','服务文档',[
 ['The service may reject requests when a client sends them too quickly. In this training API, a rate-limit response includes a wait_seconds field. Pause for at least that long before attempting the request again. This value describes the earliest suggested retry time, not a guarantee that the next request will succeed. Other clients using the same account may still be consuming the shared allowance.','客户端发送请求过快时，服务可能拒绝请求。在此练习 API 中，限流响应包含 wait_seconds 字段。至少暂停这么长时间后再重试。这个值表示建议的最早重试时间，而不是保证下一次请求一定成功。使用同一账户的其他客户端可能仍在消耗共享额度。'],
 ['Avoid immediate, unlimited retries. They can increase the load while giving the server little time to recover. Set a retry limit and show a useful message if the operation still cannot be completed. Where possible, spread repeated background work over time rather than making every client retry at exactly the same moment.','避免立即、无限次重试。这会增加负载，却不给服务器足够恢复时间。设置重试上限，如果操作仍无法完成，应显示有用提示。可行时，将重复后台任务分散到不同时间，而不是让每个客户端在完全相同的时刻重试。'],
 ['Be especially careful when retrying an operation that creates or changes data. A connection failure does not always tell you whether the first attempt reached the server. Before resending a payment or an order, consult the endpoint documentation for its duplicate-prevention mechanism. Retrying a read and repeating a purchase are not interchangeable decisions.','重试创建或修改数据的操作时尤其要小心。连接失败并不总能说明首次尝试是否已经到达服务器。重新发送付款或订单之前，请查看接口文档中的防重复机制。重试读取和重复购买不是可以等同处理的决策。']
],[['rate limit','请求速率限制','The client reached the rate limit.'],['at least that long','至少那么长时间','Pause for at least that long.'],['shared allowance','共享额度','Other clients use the same shared allowance.'],['retry limit','重试上限','Set a retry limit.'],['duplicate prevention','防止重复','Check the duplicate-prevention mechanism.']],[[
 '等待指定时间是否保证下次成功？',['保证','不保证，其他客户端也可能使用额度','保证所有后续请求免费'],1,'第一段明确区分 earliest suggested time 和 guarantee。'],['为什么不应无限立即重试？',['会增加负载且不给恢复时间','会自动删除服务器','重试次数越多文字越长'],0,'第二段说明了负载和恢复时间。'],['付款请求连接失败后，为什么不能直接反复发送？',['第一次可能已到服务器，需防重复','付款永远不能使用网络','读取和购买始终完全一样'],0,'第三段关注结果不确定和重复操作风险。']
],{task:'为团队写一段请求重试策略的说明。',audience:'实现客户端的同事',length:'110～160 词',requirements:['说明最短等待与有限重试','说明不能承诺重试必然成功','区分读取与修改数据的操作'],starter:'When the service returns…\nFor operations that change data,…',model:'When the service returns a rate-limit response, we should wait for at least the duration in wait_seconds before trying again. This is a minimum suggested delay, not a promise of success, because other clients may share the account allowance. We should use a limited number of retries and provide a clear message when the operation remains unavailable. Background clients should avoid retrying at exactly the same moment. For operations that change data, we also need to consider whether the first attempt may already have reached the server. Before retrying a payment or order, check the endpoint’s duplicate-prevention mechanism. We should not apply a read-request policy to purchases without reviewing those differences.'});
U('review-comment',1,'代码审查：建议还是必须修改','代码审查',[
 ['Thanks for the change. The new helper makes the parsing code easier to follow. I have one blocking concern and two optional suggestions. The blocking concern is that an empty input now produces a successful result with an empty identifier. Our callers currently use a successful result to mean that an identifier was found, so this change could make them act on invalid data. Please either preserve the previous failure behaviour or update the contract and its callers explicitly.','感谢修改。新辅助函数使解析代码更容易理解。我有一个阻塞合并的问题和两个可选建议。阻塞问题是：空输入现在会产生成功结果，但标识符为空。现有调用方用成功结果表示已找到标识符，因此这个变动可能导致它们对无效数据采取操作。请保留之前的失败行为，或明确更新约定及调用方。'],
 ['The optional suggestions concern naming and layout. I would prefer a name that includes “identifier”, because “value” could refer to several different things here. You might also move the short validation check above the parsing branch. Neither suggestion needs to block this patch if the team prefers the current style.','可选建议涉及命名和布局。我倾向于在名称中包含 identifier，因为这里 value 可能指多种不同内容。你也可以将简短的验证检查移到解析分支之前。如果团队倾向当前风格，这两个建议都不必阻塞此次修改。'],
 ['Could you add a test for the empty-input case and explain which behaviour you chose? I have not reviewed the separate performance changes yet. My comments on this file should not be read as approval of the entire patch. Once the contract issue is resolved, I can review the remaining changes.','能否为空输入情况添加测试，并解释你选择哪种行为？我还没有审查单独的性能改动。我对这个文件的评论不应被理解为批准整个补丁。约定问题解决后，我可以继续审查其他改动。']
],[['blocking concern','阻塞处理的问题','There is one blocking concern.'],['caller','调用方','Update the callers explicitly.'],['preserve','保留','Preserve the previous behaviour.'],['optional suggestion','可选建议','The naming change is an optional suggestion.'],['should not be read as','不应被理解为','This comment should not be read as approval.']],[[
 '真正阻塞合并的是什么？',['名称不够漂亮','空输入被错误地当作成功','验证检查的位置'],1,'第一段明确标记 blocking concern。'],['命名建议必须修改才能合并吗？',['文中说必须','文中说可选，不必阻塞','必须把所有名称改为 value'],1,'第二段的 Neither suggestion needs to block 明确了程度。'],['审查者是否已批准全部补丁？',['已批准','没有，性能部分尚未审查','已经完成部署'],1,'第三段限定审查覆盖范围。']
],{task:'回复这条代码审查，说明你如何处理阻塞问题及可选建议。',audience:'代码审查者',length:'100～150 词',requirements:['明确空输入的处理决定','提到针对性测试','将可选风格调整与未审部分分开'],starter:'Thanks for pointing out…\nI have changed…',model:'Thanks for pointing out the contract issue. I have restored the previous failure behaviour for empty input, so callers will not receive a successful result with an empty identifier. I also added a test for that case and checked that valid input still returns the expected identifier. I accepted the naming suggestion because the more specific name helps explain the helper’s purpose. I left the validation check in its current position to keep this patch focused, but I am happy to discuss that separately. I understand that the performance changes have not been reviewed yet. Please take another look at the contract fix when you have time.'});
U('deadline-message',1,'延期说明：别只说“可能晚一点”','项目邮件',[
 ['I wanted to let you know that the import guide will not be ready for review on Thursday morning as planned. During testing, I found that the current instructions skip a required confirmation step. This affects the example screenshots as well as the written procedure. I need to correct both before asking the team to review them; otherwise we would spend review time discussing instructions that I already know are incomplete.','我想提前告诉你，导入指南无法按计划在周四上午进入审查。测试中我发现，当前说明遗漏了一个必要的确认步骤，这同时影响示例截图和文字流程。请团队审查前，我需要先修正两者，否则会让大家花时间审查我已经知道不完整的说明。'],
 ['I expect to send a corrected draft by Friday at noon. That estimate assumes the revised example works in today’s test. If it does not, I will send an update by the end of today rather than waiting until Friday. The introduction and the account setup section are already ready, so you can review those now if that would help your schedule.','我预计周五中午前发送修正草稿。这个估计以修改后的示例通过今天测试为前提。如果未通过，我会在今天结束前更新情况，而不是等到周五。引言和账户设置部分已经准备好，如果有助于你的安排，可以现在先审查这些部分。'],
 ['Could you confirm whether Friday noon still leaves enough time before publication? If not, we can discuss publishing the setup section first and adding the import procedure later. I do not want to promise a complete guide until the missing step has been checked.','能否确认周五中午是否仍能为发布前准备留下足够时间？如果不能，我们可以讨论先发布设置部分，之后再补导入流程。在遗漏步骤经过验证之前，我不想承诺提供完整指南。']
],[['as planned','按计划','The draft will not be ready as planned.'],['required step','必要步骤','The guide skips a required step.'],['that estimate assumes','该估计以……为前提','That estimate assumes today’s test passes.'],['by the end of today','今天结束前','I will send an update by the end of today.'],['leave enough time','留出足够时间','Does Friday leave enough time for review?']],[[
 '延期原因是什么？',['作者不想让人审查','发现说明缺少必要步骤','引言尚未开始'],1,'第一段解释了测试发现及影响。'],['周五中午的估计是否无条件保证？',['是','不是，依赖当天测试结果','意味着已经发布'],1,'第二段用 assumes 标明条件。'],['测试失败时何时更新情况？',['周五之后','今天结束前','永不更新'],1,'rather than waiting until Friday 进一步排除错误理解。']
],{task:'写一封延期说明，给出具体影响、新估计和备选方案。',audience:'等待你交付材料的同事',length:'110～160 词',requirements:['说明原计划与阻碍','给出带条件的新时间和下次更新节点','提供可先交付部分或备选方案'],starter:'The draft will not be ready…\nI expect… provided that…',model:'The draft will not be ready for review on Thursday morning as planned. Testing revealed a missing confirmation step, so both the instructions and the screenshots need changes. I expect to send a corrected draft by Friday noon, provided that the revised example works in today’s test. If it fails, I will update you before the end of today. The introduction and account setup section are already complete and can be reviewed separately. Could you confirm whether Friday noon leaves enough time before publication? If the full guide is needed earlier, we could publish the setup section first and add the import instructions after testing. I would prefer to agree on that reduced scope rather than promise an unchecked procedure.'});
U('meeting-followup',1,'会后邮件：决定、行动和未决事项','会议纪要',[
 ['Thanks for the discussion today. We agreed to test the new request form with the support team before making it available to all users. This is a limited trial, not approval for a full launch. The trial will use sample requests with no customer details. Lena will prepare the form, and I will write the short instructions that explain when the form should be used. Both items are due by Wednesday afternoon.','感谢今天的讨论。我们同意先与支持团队测试新申请表，再考虑向所有用户开放。这是有限试用，并非批准全面发布。试用使用不含客户信息的示例申请。Lena 准备表单，我负责简短说明，解释何时应该使用。两项任务都应在周三下午前完成。'],
 ['One question remains open: should users receive a copy of their submitted request? We discussed two options but did not make a decision. Omar will ask the support team which option would reduce follow-up work and share the findings on Thursday. Until we decide, please do not add an automatic email step to the launch plan.','一个问题仍未决定：用户是否应收到自己已提交申请的副本？我们讨论了两个选项，但没有决策。Omar 会询问支持团队哪个选项能减少后续工作，并在周四分享结果。决定之前，请不要将自动邮件步骤加入发布计划。'],
 ['After the trial, we will review whether participants understood the instructions and whether the form collected enough information. We have not set a public launch date. Please reply if I have recorded an owner, deadline or decision incorrectly. Silence on this email should not be treated as confirmation that every open question has been resolved.','试用后，我们会检查参与者是否理解说明，以及表单是否收集到足够信息。公开发布日期尚未确定。如果我记录错了负责人、截止时间或决定，请回复指出。没有人回复这封邮件，不应被理解为所有未决问题都已解决。']
],[['limited trial','有限试用','We agreed to a limited trial.'],['due by','应在……之前完成','The instructions are due by Wednesday.'],['remain open','仍未解决','One question remains open.'],['follow-up work','后续处理工作','The form should reduce follow-up work.'],['be treated as','被视为','Silence should not be treated as approval.']],[[
 '会上批准了什么？',['全面发布','与支持团队做有限试用','公开上线日期'],1,'第一段明确区分 trial 与 full launch。'],['邮件自动发送功能已经决定了吗？',['已经决定必须做','尚未决定','已决定永远不做'],1,'第二段说讨论过但没有作出决定。'],['作者邀请收件人核对什么？',['负责人、时间和决定','客户密码','所有人的私人安排'],0,'第三段列出了 owner、deadline、decision。']
],{task:'把一次虚构会议整理成会后邮件。',audience:'会议参与者',length:'110～160 词',requirements:['记录一个已决定事项','写清两项行动的负责人和时间','标记一个未决问题，避免把讨论当批准'],starter:'We agreed to…\nAction items:\nStill open:',model:'Thanks for today’s discussion. We agreed to run a small trial of the new request form with the support team. This does not approve a public launch. Lena will prepare the form by Wednesday afternoon, and I will finish the user instructions by the same time. We will use sample requests without customer details. One question remains open: whether users should receive a copy of each submitted request. Omar will collect the support team’s feedback and share it on Thursday. Please do not add automatic confirmation emails to the plan until we make that decision. After the trial, we will review the instructions and the information collected. Please correct any owner, deadline or decision I have recorded incorrectly.'});
U('access-request',1,'申请权限：范围、理由和期限','工作邮件',[
 ['Could you grant me read access to the sample reporting project until the end of next week? I am checking whether the new export guide matches the interface. I only need to view the sample reports and their settings. I do not need access to live customer data, billing information or account administration. If a separate demonstration project already covers these screens, access to that project would be sufficient.','能否授予我示例报告项目的只读权限，到下周末为止？我正在检查新导出指南是否与界面一致，只需要查看示例报告及其设置。我不需要访问真实客户数据、账单信息或账户管理。如果已有独立演示项目覆盖这些界面，访问那个项目也足够。'],
 ['I expect to finish the check by Thursday, but I have requested access through next week in case the guide needs a second review. Once the work is complete, I will let you know so the access can be removed earlier. Please do not send shared credentials in an email reply. An invitation to my work account is the preferred method.','我预计周四完成检查，但申请权限延续到下周，以便指南需要二次审查时使用。工作完成后我会通知你，以便提前移除权限。请不要通过邮件回复发送共享登录凭据，优先邀请我的工作账户。'],
 ['If the request needs approval from a project owner, please tell me who should review it. I can provide the documentation task number and a list of the screens I need to check. I am asking for the minimum access required for this task, rather than a permanent role in the production project.','如果申请需要项目负责人批准，请告诉我应由谁审核。我可以提供文档任务编号和需要检查的界面清单。我申请的是完成这项任务所需的最小权限，而不是生产项目中的永久角色。']
],[['read access','只读访问权限','I only need read access.'],['sufficient','足够的','A demonstration project would be sufficient.'],['in case','以防；以备','Keep access in case a second review is needed.'],['shared credentials','共享登录凭据','Do not send shared credentials by email.'],['minimum required','所需的最低限度','Request the minimum required access.']],[[
 '作者真正需要哪类权限？',['生产系统永久管理员','查看示例报告及设置的权限','所有客户账单的写权限'],1,'首段明确范围并列出不需要的内容。'],['如果演示项目覆盖所需界面，可以使用它吗？',['可以','不可以，必须真实客户数据','必须同时获取所有项目'],0,'would be sufficient 表示足以满足任务。'],['任务提前结束时，作者承诺什么？',['继续永久保留权限','通知对方以便提前移除','把密码转给朋友'],1,'第二段说明完成后通知移除。']
],{task:'为一项文档检查任务写权限申请。',audience:'项目负责人',length:'100～150 词',requirements:['明确任务、权限范围和期限','说明不需要的敏感范围或可接受的替代环境','给出结束后的权限处理和正确邀请方式'],starter:'I am working on…\nCould you grant… until…?',model:'I am checking the export instructions for our reporting guide. Could you grant my work account read access to the sample reporting project until the end of next week? I need to view the report screens and their settings, but I do not need customer data, billing details or administration permissions. A separate demonstration project would also be sufficient if it contains the same screens. I expect to finish by Thursday and will let you know when access can be removed. Please send an account invitation rather than shared credentials. If another project owner must approve this request, I can provide the task number and the list of screens for review.'});
U('subscription-renewal',1,'取消续费与立即终止服务','订阅说明',[
 ['Your annual subscription is scheduled to renew on 18 June. If you do not want another annual term, turn off automatic renewal before that date. In this example service, turning it off does not immediately remove paid features. You can continue using them until the end of the period you have already paid for. Cancelling renewal is therefore different from requesting immediate account closure.','你的年度订阅计划在六月十八日续费。如果不希望开始下一年度，请在该日期之前关闭自动续费。在这个示例服务中，关闭续费不会立即移除付费功能，你可以继续使用到已付费周期结束。因此，取消续费不同于要求立即注销账户。'],
 ['After the paid period ends, your account moves to the free plan. Existing files remain available for download for thirty days, but you cannot create new projects above the free-plan limit. Download any files you want to keep before that window closes. The thirty-day download window is not an extension of the paid plan and does not include its editing features.','付费周期结束后，账户转为免费方案。现有文件仍可下载三十天，但不能创建超出免费额度的新项目。请在这个期限结束前下载要保留的文件。这三十天下载期不等于延长付费方案，也不包含付费编辑功能。'],
 ['If your subscription was purchased through a separate marketplace, manage renewal through that provider rather than this page. The account page shows which provider handles your billing. Contact support if the provider information is missing, and keep the cancellation confirmation for your records.','如果订阅通过独立市场购买，请通过该提供商管理续费，而不是在本页操作。账户页面会显示账单由哪家提供商处理。如果该信息缺失，请联系支持，并保留取消确认记录。']
],[['automatic renewal','自动续费','Turn off automatic renewal before the renewal date.'],['paid period','已付费周期','Features remain available during the paid period.'],['account closure','账户注销','Renewal cancellation is not immediate account closure.'],['download window','可下载期限','Save your files before the download window closes.'],['billing provider','账单服务提供商','Check which billing provider manages the subscription.']],[[
 '本例关闭自动续费后，付费功能何时结束？',['立即','已付费周期结束时','永不结束'],1,'第一段明确 until the end of the period already paid for。'],['三十天下载期是否包含完整付费编辑功能？',['包含','不包含','等于再免费续一年'],1,'第二段专门排除这一理解。'],['通过独立市场购买，在哪里管理续费？',['通过对应提供商','随便删除本地快捷方式','在任何网页留言即可'],0,'第三段限定购买渠道对应的管理方式。']
],{task:'回复朋友，解释如何取消下一年续费但暂时保留本年度使用。',audience:'朋友',length:'100～150 词',requirements:['区分取消续费与注销账户','说明付费期和下载期的不同权限','提醒按购买渠道操作并保留确认'],starter:'You can turn off… without…\nAfter the paid period,…',model:'In this service, you can turn off automatic renewal without closing your account immediately. Do it before the renewal date, and you can keep using paid features until the current paid period ends. After that, the account moves to the free plan. There is a thirty-day window for downloading existing files, but that does not extend the paid editing features. I suggest saving important files before the window closes. Also check who handles your billing. If you purchased through a separate marketplace, manage renewal with that provider rather than this page. Keep the cancellation confirmation so you have a record of the change.'});
U('travel-change',1,'行程变更：取消一段会影响什么','出行通知',[
 ['Your train service on Saturday has been cancelled. You may choose a replacement service on the same route at no additional fare, subject to seat availability, or request a refund for the affected journey. Your reservation will not automatically move to another train. Please select a replacement before travelling and keep the updated confirmation with you.','你周六的列车服务已取消。可以在有座位的前提下，免费选择同一路线的替代车次，或申请受影响行程的退款。原预约不会自动转移到另一趟列车。出行前请选择替代车次，并携带更新确认。'],
 ['If your booking includes a separate return journey, cancelling the outbound journey does not automatically cancel the return. Check both entries in your booking before confirming a refund request. If the two journeys were purchased as a package from another seller, contact that seller to ask how a partial cancellation affects the remaining booking. The options on this page apply only to tickets bought directly from us.','如果订单中包含独立回程，取消去程不会自动取消回程。确认退款申请前，请检查订单中的两项行程。如果两段行程通过其他卖家作为套餐购买，请联系该卖家，询问部分取消如何影响剩余订单。本页选项只适用于直接向我们购买的车票。'],
 ['We cannot confirm connections operated by other companies. If the replacement train arrives later, check any onward journey separately before accepting it. A refund for this train does not necessarily include the cost of a hotel or another operator’s ticket. Please keep receipts and ask the relevant provider which conditions apply to those separate purchases.','我们无法确认其他公司运营的接续交通。如果替代车次到达更晚，请在接受前另外检查后续行程。这趟列车退款不一定包含酒店或其他运营商车票的费用。请保留收据，并向相关提供商确认这些独立购买适用的条件。']
],[['subject to availability','视供应情况而定','Replacement seats are subject to availability.'],['affected journey','受影响的行程','Request a refund for the affected journey.'],['outbound journey','去程','The outbound journey has been cancelled.'],['onward journey','后续行程','Check your onward journey separately.'],['not necessarily include','不一定包括','The refund does not necessarily include hotel costs.']],[[
 '原座位会自动转到其他列车吗？',['会','不会，需要选择替代车次','会转到最贵车次'],1,'第一段说 reservation will not automatically move。'],['独立预订的回程会随着去程取消吗？',['自动取消','不会自动取消','必须从此不能使用'],1,'第二段明确区分两项预订。'],['火车退款一定包含酒店费用吗？',['一定','不一定，要查相关购买条件','包括所有旅行消费'],1,'第三段用 not necessarily 限定退款范围。']
],{task:'给客服写信，确认去程取消后的改签和回程安排。',audience:'交通服务客服',length:'110～160 词',requirements:['说明受影响行程和希望采用的替代方案','明确询问回程是否保留','提到后续接续安排需要确认，避免默认全额补偿'],starter:'My Saturday service…\nBefore I choose…',model:'My Saturday service has been cancelled, and I would like to choose a replacement on the same route. Before I confirm a new train, could you tell me which services still have seats? My booking also includes a separate return journey that I want to keep. Please confirm that changing the outbound journey will not cancel the return. The replacement must also leave enough time for a connection operated by another company. I understand that I need to check that connection separately and that a refund for this train may not cover other expenses. Please send an updated confirmation once the replacement is arranged. I will check the date and arrival time before travelling.'});
